      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1294339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-23T08:09:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg, according to the conclusion by https://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/u/3/issues/228783879, this patch is aimed to fix MediaTek MCQ solution in Android13-5.15. The MCQ feature adopted in Android13-5.15 adopted is MediaTek\u0027s implementation of early MCQ specification (not fully compatible to final standard anyway) so it is not suitable to be upstreamed.",
      "parentUuid": "5fda5bb7_e3ae6369",
      "revId": "b4e36980d158254f754cc015d8e6b265ba7b5771",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddd1de54_7e3c27d9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-23T08:17:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "non-standard hardware is supported upstream every day.  That\u0027s never an excuse to not get the needed changes merged, it should be easy to do with a device quirk.",
      "parentUuid": "e1a9d148_33fb076d",
      "revId": "b4e36980d158254f754cc015d8e6b265ba7b5771",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1659b641_ee635e39",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1294339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-24T02:39:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg, we certainly try to upstream this MCQ implementation later because our current product adopting this MCQ implementation may need to align the mainline after future kernel migration.\n\nHowever the upstream is too late for our product using ACK13-5.15 currently regarding to the time to market. Our customers now need this MCQ implementation and following fixes.\n\nPlease kindly consider this special situation. Thanks.",
      "parentUuid": "ddd1de54_7e3c27d9",
      "revId": "b4e36980d158254f754cc015d8e6b265ba7b5771",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed36730a_33ff1258",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-24T08:12:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please submit it upstream first now, we can easily backport quirks to this tree if they are accepted there.",
      "parentUuid": "1659b641_ee635e39",
      "revId": "b4e36980d158254f754cc015d8e6b265ba7b5771",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3963d78a_be4dba69",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1294339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-24T13:07:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg, be honestly, we can not upstream \"exactly the same\" MCQ implementation because we re-organized this patch specifically for ACK13-5.15 earlier to not hack too much common code. This \nis a compromised way in that time because ACK13-5.15 KMI freeze date was very closed but customer need this feature in MTK platform. Now we have to stay at this version and try to fix any bugs to make customer MP successful.",
      "parentUuid": "ed36730a_33ff1258",
      "revId": "b4e36980d158254f754cc015d8e6b265ba7b5771",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d2526d08_40f9fa20",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-24T13:11:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t say to submit the \"same\" code, do it properly upstream first, and then we can work on a correct way to backport it here.\n\nTHe 5.15 KMI freeze for `android13` is long past, that should not affect anything here as you are not changing any abi.  If your upstream change does modify the ABI, then we will be glad to revisit it at that point in time.",
      "parentUuid": "3963d78a_be4dba69",
      "revId": "b4e36980d158254f754cc015d8e6b265ba7b5771",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
